\section{Proof appendix: complete arguments for the current lemma chain}\label{sec:proofappendix}
This section proves the implications labeled PROVED and the implication part of each CONDITIONAL lemma.  Raw exact-rational or interval arithmetic is delegated only where explicitly stated.

\subsection{Shipping OU prediction identities}
For one OU axis,
\[
a_w(t+s)=e^{-s/\tau}a_w(t)+\int_0^s e^{-(s-r)/\tau}\,dW(r).
\]
Successive integration gives the deterministic coefficients multiplying the root acceleration. With \(x=h/\tau\),
\[
\phi_{pa}=\tau^2(x+e^{-x}-1),\qquad
\phi_{Sa}=\tau^3(\tfrac12x^2-x-e^{-x}+1).
\]
Taylor expansion identifies the ideal limits. Shipping uses finite
small-\(x\) polynomials, whose nonzero remainder must remain explicit. The process covariance has Gram form
\[
Q=\int_0^h\Phi(h-s)LL^T\Phi(h-s)^T\,ds\succeq0.
\]
The literal small-$x$ covariance is compared with this ideal Gram, rather
than equated to it. The rational coefficient/tail calculation in
\texttt{lin\_path\_certificate.small\_x\_source\_defect} uses natural
step scaling $D_h=\operatorname{diag}(h,h^2,h^3,1)$ and gives
$Q_{\rm ship}\succeq(1-\epsilon_Q)Q_{\rm ideal}$ with
$0\le\epsilon_Q<1$ on the qualified domain. It also charges the nonzero
$\Delta\Phi$ in the path action. The reproduced LIN matrix certificate
retains these terms, establishing the stated real-arithmetic PSD comparison.
No exact-real or float32 branch is silently substituted for another.

\subsection{Joseph correction and reset action}
For \(S=HP^-H^T+R\), \(K=P^-H^TS^{-1}\), \(A=I-KH\),
\[
P^+=AP^-A^T+KRK^T
=P^- -P^-H^TS^{-1}HP^-.
\]
The Woodbury identity yields the equivalent positive information increment. Hence correction action is nonnegative and zero action implies zero corresponding whitened homogeneous innovation. The certificate evaluates this identity with the literal matrices and retains cross covariance.

If \(e^+=Ge\) and \(P^+=GP^-G^T\), then
\[
(e^+)^T(P^+)^{-1}e^+=e^T(P^-)^{-1}e
\]
for nonsingular \(G\). Therefore the shipping reset transports storage but creates no artificial loss or supply.

\subsection{Held BA and loss of heading service}
On a held-BA interval the estimator BA mean is constant, its gain rows vanish and its covariance block is frozen/decoupled. For two perturbations sharing one physical bias history,
\[
\delta e_o^+=A\delta e_o+B\delta e_b,\qquad
\delta e_b^+=\delta e_b,
\]
so
\[
\Psi=\begin{bmatrix}A&B\\0&I_3\end{bmatrix}.
\]
Thus strict full-state H18 contraction in a fixed positive quadratic metric is impossible and is not a premise of the proof.

Without informative heading service the axial equations satisfy
\[
\dot\theta_z=-e_{b_g,z},\qquad \dot e_{b_g,z}=0,
\]
hence over \(T\)
\[
\binom{\theta_z(T)}{e_{b_g,z}(T)}
=\begin{bmatrix}1&-T\\0&1\end{bmatrix}
\binom{\theta_z(0)}{e_{b_g,z}(0)}.
\]
The nontrivial Jordan block gives linear heading growth for nonzero axial bias error, proving the necessity of recurring magnetic service.

\subsection{Qualified gyro-bias alias exclusion}
A sampled complete-turn alias requires an integer \(2\pi\) nominal rotation within one prediction step. On the qualified \(4\)--\(6\) ms family the implemented \(\norm{\hat b_g}\le0.5\) projection together with the physical slow/FAST gyro and angular-rate envelopes gives a one-step angle strictly below the first nonzero complete turn. The committed interval certificate checks the worst endpoint and a positive transverse singular floor. Therefore the alias is excluded on this qualified timestep family.

\subsection{Complete-word LIN and joint kernel reduction}
Zero process action places the homogeneous root in the exact kernel of every transported process factor. Zero \(S\)-correction action adds the transported \(S\) rows. Stacking these literal rows at a common root and eliminating along \(v\to p\to S\) removes independent LIN/\(a_w\) zero-action roots. The certificate performs exact rational row reduction, not a floating rank threshold.

Condition on a fixed admissible complete magnetic/event transport stratum. After LIN reduction, zero magnetic action restricts AG to the service-compatible subspace; literal accelerometer rows then impose BA compatibility. Exact reduction of this complete stack gives nullity at most one on every certified stratum. This proves the conditional implication. The open premise is a continuous source-uniform cover of every reachable MAGNETIC SERVICE row/transport stratum.

At an active A21 accelerometer update the BA Jacobian block is \(I_3\) up to the residual sign convention. Therefore, once a surviving attitude amplitude is fixed, \(H_{\rm acc}e=0\) has at most one BA solution. BA cannot add an independent kernel direction.

\subsection{Same-history physical-to-nominal bridge}
Assume a nonzero compatibility direction persists through a qualified moving superword. Transporting the literal zero-innovation equations to common world coordinates removes absolute attitude from same-cell force/field geometry. Slow bias terms retain their amplitude/rate histories, FAST terms retain their signed primitives, physical acceleration is tied to the same \(v\)-history by \(v'=a\) and the jerk bound, and magnetic rows use the same accepted service history. Persistence therefore implies vanishing of the linked A* physical/nominal functional. The derived A* inequality excludes persistence whenever its source margin is strictly positive. The implication is proved; the open premise is a source-uniform positive margin on every reachable physical HistoryCell and prefix.

\subsection{H18 release and A21 root covariance}
Assume finite completion of the shipping reference-refinement/release state machine. Captured attitude, projected gyro bias and held BA are compact/bounded; the literal H18 LIN subsystem is BIBO with BA as bounded input; tuner/reference/scheduler/covariance maps are continuous over the finite bridge. Hence the terminal release image is compact. The unresolved premise is source-uniform finite completion of that state machine.

For recurring A21 roots, the exact-rational LIN certificate proves a full Loewner lower comparison for the complete \(16\)-s LIN path. The joint-root certificate combines this with fresh AG/BA process injection while retaining cross covariance and proves
\[
P_{\rm root}\succeq L_{\rm root}\succ0.
\]
The finite certificate checks exact rational LDL/Loewner inequalities; only raw arithmetic is delegated. Since inversion reverses Loewner order,
\[
J_{\rm root}=P_{\rm root}^{-1}\preceq L_{\rm root}^{-1}.
\]
If the release image is compact, continuity of \(V=e^TJe\) then gives a finite \(C_{\rm out}=\sup V\), proving existence of a compact outer root region. Retention and inner entry remain separate open premises.

\subsection{Specific-force and quaternion normalization}
Reverse triangle inequality gives
\[
\norm{f_{\rm raw}}\ge g-A_{\max}-B_{a,s}-B_{a,f}>0.
\]
No component independence is used.

For \(r=\frac{\Delta t}{2}(0,\omega_c)\), quaternion multiplication by the pure imaginary \(r\) is orthogonal to \(q\) in \(\R^4\), and
\(\norm{q\otimes r}=\norm q\,\norm r\). Hence
\[
\norm{q+q\otimes r}^2
=\norm q^2(1+\norm r^2)
=\norm q^2\left(1+\frac{\Delta t^2}{4}\norm{\omega_c}^2\right).
\]
Thus Cartesian quaternion intervals cannot create a physical zero normalization denominator.

\subsection{Vibration guard and FAST Abel state}
For one pole,
\[
s_k=(1-\alpha)f_k+\alpha s_{k-1}.
\]
With \(d_k=s_k-f_k\),
\[
d_k=\alpha(d_{k-1}-(f_k-f_{k-1})),
\]
so
\[
\norm{d_k}\le\alpha(\norm{d_{k-1}}+\Delta_k).
\]
Repeating the subtraction through the positive cascade proves the stated later-pole recurrence. Since \(f_c=f+w d_{\rm LP}\),
\[
\norm{f_c}\ge\norm f-w_{\max}\norm{d_{\rm LP}}.
\]

For FAST input write the current finite causal LP-minus-identity state as
\[
d_k=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}q_j u_{k-j}.
\]
Let \(U_m=h\sum_{i\le m}u_i\). Discrete Abel summation rewrites \(d_k\) as endpoint primitive terms plus first differences \(q_{j+1}-q_j\). The all-placed-window primitive cap bounds those terms by \(C_a/h\), while the stable pre-horizon tail is charged by \(B_{a,f}\). This charge is applied once to the current LP state, not recursively at each sample. Taking its minimum with the valid pointwise \(2B_{a,f}\) bound preserves rigor.

\subsection{Integrated weighted guard--reader Abel bound}
For
\[
Q=h\sum_k c_kw_k[(L-I)u]_k,
\]
expand the convolution and interchange the finite sums to obtain
\[
Q=h\sum_j q_j u_j.
\]
Using \(U_j=h\sum_{i\le j}u_i\), Abel summation gives, up to the endpoint convention,
\[
Q=q_NU_N+\sum_j(q_j-q_{j+1})U_j.
\]
Therefore
\[
|Q|\le C_a\left(|q_N|+\sum_j|q_{j+1}-q_j|\right).
\]
The \(h\) in the integrated functional cancels the primitive \(1/h\). In the interval certificate \(q_j\) is constructed only after pairing same-sample reader and guard-weight cells, including the bilinear radius term, so no independent global supremum product is introduced.

\subsection{Backward interval AW reader}
Start with terminal row \(\lambda_N\). Reverse a prediction by
\(\lambda^-=\lambda^+F\). Reverse a correction
\[
e^+=(I-KH)e^-+Kr_{\rm src}
\]
by recording source coefficient \(\lambda^+K\) and propagating
\[
\lambda^-=\lambda^+(I-KH).
\]
Forward reset follows correction, so reverse chronology crosses \(G\) first. Midpoint-radius products include
\[
|\bar\lambda|\,\Delta M+\Delta\lambda\,|\bar M|
+\Delta\lambda\,\Delta M,
\]
which encloses every product in the event cell. Backward induction therefore encloses every \(c_k=\lambda_k^TK_k\).

\subsection{Physical HistoryCell subdivision}
A root HistoryCell contains only declared physical/sensor coordinates. Bisection of one interval creates two children whose union is exactly the parent physical set. Regenerating the complete causal estimator history in each child preserves the functional dependence of every generated state on that physical history. Induction over the subdivision tree proves coverage. Because generated quantities are not root coordinates, the cover cannot manufacture impossible independent combinations of \(w,\tau,R_S,P,K\), Mahony state or scheduler state.

\subsection{Linked finite-error completed square}
Let
\[
e_N=Me_0+b,\qquad V_0=e_0^TJ_0e_0,\qquad V_N=e_N^TJ_Ne_N.
\]
For \(0<\gamma\) define
\[
G_\gamma=J_0-M^TJ_NM-\gamma J_0,\qquad z=M^TJ_Nb.
\]
If \(G_\gamma\succ0\), direct expansion gives
\[
V_N-(1-\gamma)V_0
=-e_0^TG_\gamma e_0+2e_0^Tz+b^TJ_Nb.
\]
Completing the square,
\[
-e_0^TG_\gamma e_0+2e_0^Tz
=-(e_0-G_\gamma^{-1}z)^TG_\gamma(e_0-G_\gamma^{-1}z)
+z^TG_\gamma^{-1}z.
\]
Hence
\[
V_N\le(1-\gamma)V_0+\chi_\gamma,\qquad
\chi_\gamma=b^TJ_Nb+z^TG_\gamma^{-1}z.
\]
Thus \(\chi_\gamma/\gamma<r^2\), together with prefix retention, implies strict entry/retention relative to the radius \(r\). Such a strict target cannot be imposed on all admitted quiet histories. The algebra does not establish its hypotheses on MOVING histories either; the planar compatibility audit must first be resolved with actual all-time magnetic service.


\subsection{Quiet fibre and persistent source charge}
For a constant quiet record, \(d=b_{s,\rm hold}+b_f\). Averaging over a complete
\(H\)-window yields \(\norm d\le B_s+C/H\). Conversely, radially project
\(d\) onto the \(B_s\) ball and put the constant remainder in FAST. Its norm
is at most \(C/H<B_f\); for every \(T\le H\) its signed integral is bounded
by both \(B_fT\) and \(C\). The split persists forever and its slow derivative
is zero. This proves necessity and sufficiency, not merely a pointwise outer box.
For \(B=y_m=75e_x\), \(R^TB=B\) gives \(R=R_x(\theta)\), and
\[
\norm{-g_me_z+gR^Te_z}^2
=(g-g_m)^2+4gg_m\sin^2(\theta/2).
\]
The physical primitive \(S_*\) is inherited; the estimator's \(S=0\) correction
does not reset physical truth.

For a centered interval \(I\) of length \(L\), contained in a quiet episode,
\[
L(d-b_s(t_k))=\int_I(d-b_{s,\rm hold})\,dt
 +\int_I(b_{s,\rm hold}-b_s(t_k))\,dt.
\]
The first integral has norm at most \(C\). The second is bounded by
\(D(L^2/4+hL)\): the centered distance integral is \(L^2/4\), and each hold
origin differs from its time by at most \(h\). Division by \(L\) proves the
charge. A one-sided interval instead gives \(DL/2\). With current constants,
\(L_a=14\), \(L_g=28\), \(h=.006\), the charges are
\(\eta_a=.00707742857143\) and \(\eta_g=.000141488571429\).
Let \(r_a=\eta_a+C_a/H_a\), \(r_g=\eta_g\) for zero gyro record.
Keeping the same attitude and inherited LIN coordinates in a constant compatible
representative changes only the physical slow-bias error coordinates. Therefore,
for \(J_{bb}=E_b^TP_k^{-1}E_b\),
\[
\operatorname{dist}_{P_k^{-1}}(e_k,\mathcal Q_{{\rm still},k})^2
\le\sup_{\norm{u_a}\le r_a,\,\norm{u_g}\le r_g}
\binom{u_g}{u_a}^{T}J_{bb}\binom{u_g}{u_a}.
\]
This is a same-prefix source projection bound. It retains cross covariance;
its uniformization and boundedness of the estimator remain separate obligations.

\subsection{Exact MOVING sensor-compatible pair}
For a fixed field-axis rotation \(Q\), put \(d_Q=(Q^T-I)ge_z\).
The transformation
\[
R_1=QR_0,\quad a_1=Qa_0,\quad
b_{a,1}=b_{a,0}+R_0^Td_Q
\]
preserves specific force and magnetic observations. The two body rates agree,
and \(\frac{d}{dt}(R_0^Td_Q)=-[\omega_0]_\times R_0^Td_Q\).
Thus bias compensation is constant when rotation is about that body vector,
although gravity direction need not be constant.

For the explicit symmetric pair, direct multiplication gives
\[
\begin{aligned}
R_\pm^T(a_xe_x-ge_z)+b_{a,\pm}&=R_y(-\psi)(a_xe_x-gce_z),\\
R_\pm^TB&=75R_y(-\psi)e_x.
\end{aligned}
\]
Also \(R_\pm^T\dot R_\pm=[\dot\psi e_y]_\times\) and
\((R_+^T-R_-^T)ge_z=2gs e_y\), proving identical records and a zero
two-epoch difference for every pair of times. This is not a homogeneous BA
solution: the physical prediction forcing \((1-\phi_b)b_a\) is retained.

Every 30-second interval contains the 20-second period. At its pitch extrema
\(\pm.02\), the gravity-direction chord is \(2c\sin(.02)\).
Using \(\sin(.02)\ge.02-.02^3/6\) proves a span larger than two degrees.
The displacement span is \(.04\). Differentiating the specified \(p\) gives
bounds below \(.006284\), \(.001975\), \(.000621\) for velocity,
acceleration and jerk; integrating gives \(\norm S<.128\).
Bias norms are \(gs=.09806404839879003<B_{a,s}\), bias rates are zero, and
FAST primitives vanish identically. Exact rational checks reproduce all margins.
No all-time accepted-information premise is inferred from these source bounds.

\subsection{Planar covariance parity and service phase}
For the exact planar record, prediction and all measurement rows preserve the
partition
\[
\begin{split}
E={}&\{\theta_y,b_{g,y},v_{x,z},p_{x,z},S_{x,z},a_{w,x,z},b_{a,x,z}\},\\
O={}&\{\theta_{x,z},b_{g,x,z},v_y,p_y,S_y,a_{w,y},b_{a,y}\}.
\end{split}
\]
The blocks have dimensions 12 and 9.  For an XZ predicted vector, the skew
attitude Jacobian maps X/Z residual rows to \(\theta_y\) and the Y row to
\(\theta_{x,z}\); the OU predictor and S selector are axis-separable, and
the Y-axis reset preserves the same partition.  Diagonal startup covariance
therefore gives zero E/O cross covariance for the exact real-arithmetic branch.

The auxiliary plus/minus service columns may be sum/difference transformed to
these parity blocks, but the shipping service condition is not replaced: each
physical \(+\) and \(-\) heading/BG pair retains its own 2-by-2 information
test.  The exact field geometry gives
\[
 \|[-75R_y(-\psi)e_x]_\times d_\pm\|=75
\]
at every phase.

A 20-s point covariance return is not a valid invariant target because the
shipping progress-preserving S scheduler does not return to the same phase.
At the carried tail \(T_S=0.1363605112\) s and the measured scheduler
coordinate differs after 20 s even though the applied \(\tau,\sigma,R_S,T_S\)
repeat to float precision.  Hence the rigorous Poincare object is a cell in
\((P_E,P_O,\text{adaptive state},\text{scheduler phase})\), not a single
covariance matrix.  The final-cycle all-IMU-root replay has service minimum
above 7, but outward interval self-inclusion and the all-time floor remain open.

\subsection{Planar admission-cell transport algebra}
The proof modules are \texttt{planar\_service\_cell.py},
\texttt{scheduler\_s\_shift\_bound.py}, and
\texttt{planar\_service\_frechet.py}.  Exact rational regressions are in
\texttt{planar-service-cell-certificate.json}; they supplement the following
algebraic proof, rather than replacing a general argument by sampled identities.

Write $\mathcal R_H(P)=P-PH^T(HPH^T+R)^{-1}HP$, $C=FPF^T+Q$,
$A=HPH^T+R$, $B=HCH^T+R$, $U=FPH^T$, and $Z=CH^T-U$.
Expanding both alternative local operation orders gives
\[
\begin{aligned}
D&=\mathcal R_H(C)-[F\mathcal R_H(P)F^T+Q]\\
 &=UA^{-1}U^T-(U+Z)B^{-1}(U+Z)^T.
\end{aligned}
\]
Use $A^{-1}-B^{-1}=A^{-1}(B-A)B^{-1}$, without commuting the matrices:
\[
\begin{aligned}
 D={}&UA^{-1}(B-A)B^{-1}U^T-UB^{-1}Z^T\\
 &-ZB^{-1}U^T-ZB^{-1}Z^T.
\end{aligned}
\]
In particular $D=[U,Z]M[U,Z]^T$ for a $2m$-dimensional symmetric core.
The literal $S$ selector has $m=2$ on the even block and $m=1$ on the odd
block, giving ranks at most four and two.  Also
\[
\begin{aligned}
Z&=[FP(F^T-I)+Q]H^T,\\
B-A&=H[(F-I)PF^T+P(F^T-I)+Q]H^T.
\end{aligned}
\]
Thus the small one-step differences remain linked before taking norms.
If $A\succeq aI$, $B\succeq bI$, $\|WU\|\le u$, $\|WZ\|\le z$,
and $\|B-A\|\le e$, then
\[
\|WDW^T\|\le u^2e/(ab)+(2uz+z^2)/b.
\]
For a declared cell $P=P_0+LEL^T$, $\|E\|\le r$, expand each occurrence
of the \emph{same} $E$ in these three factors and use submultiplicativity.
This proves the implemented cell formula. Its floating evaluation is not an
outward-rounded certificate and the cell is not presumed reachable.

The old implication $P\preceq\bar P\Rightarrow
\|PH^T\|\le\|\bar P H^T\|$ is false.  An exact example is
\[
\begin{gathered}
P=\begin{bmatrix}5000&5/2\\5/2&1/200\end{bmatrix},\quad H=[0,1],\\
\bar P=\operatorname{diag}(10000,1/100),\quad F=I,\\
Q=\operatorname{diag}(0,1/100),\quad R=1/100.
\end{gathered}
\]
Both $P$ and $\bar P-P$ are positive definite, but $D_{11}=500/3$,
whereas the old two-term formula gives $1/20$.  The corrected two-term
bound instead uses the PSD block Cauchy inequality
$\|FPH^T\|^2\le\|F\bar PF^T\|\|H\bar PH^T\|$.
Likewise an orientation-free accelerometer information majorant must use
\[
\Big\|\sum_i A_i x_i\Big\|^2
\le\Big(\sum_i w_i\Big)\sum_iw_i\|x_i\|^2,
\qquad \|A_i\|\le w_i,
\]
not $(ww^T)\otimes I$, which has false null directions for differently
rotated blocks. This corrected block-diagonal majorant is an explicit
relaxation; it is not used in place of the exported actual accelerometer row.
The vertical $S$ noise floor is also multiplied by the literal axis factors
$(0.72,0.50,1)$ before forming an information ceiling.

For the default AW-floor operation let $E_w$ inject the AW coordinates:
\[
\mathcal F_\Sigma(P)=P+E_w(\Sigma-P_{ww})_+E_w^T.
\]
This map is not Loewner monotone.  With one AW coordinate (coordinate two),
$P_0=I_2$, $P_1=I_2+\mathbf1\mathbf1^T$, and target $3$, its output
difference is $\left[\begin{smallmatrix}1&1\\1&0\end{smallmatrix}\right]$,
whose determinant is $-1$, although the input difference is PSD.
Consequently AW synchronization cannot be added to a monotone-face tube by
mapping its two faces independently.

There is nevertheless an exact useful norm bound. The AW output block is
$\Sigma+(P_{ww}-\Sigma)_+$.  Orthogonal projection onto the closed PSD cone
is Frobenius nonexpansive: the two projection variational inequalities imply
$\|\Pi X-\Pi Y\|_F^2\le\langle\Pi X-\Pi Y,X-Y\rangle$.
All other covariance blocks are unchanged. Summing their squared Frobenius
norms proves
\[
\|\mathcal F_\Sigma(P)-\mathcal F_\Sigma(P_0)\|_F\le\|P-P_0\|_F.
\]
Varying the target adds at most $\|\Sigma-\Sigma_0\|_F$ by the same
projection inequality and the triangle inequality. The result remains valid
under block-diagonal coordinate scaling that is scalar on each invariant AW
block; an arbitrary covariance-whitening matrix need not have this property.

For fixed $F,Q,H,R,G,\Sigma$, differentiation gives respectively
$E\mapsto FEF^T$, $E\mapsto(I-KH)E(I-KH)^T$, and $E\mapsto GEG^T$.
On a fully active AW face $\Sigma-P_{ww}\succ0$, the AW derivative deletes
only the $ww$ marginal of $E$; all cross-state covariance perturbations remain.
Composition on orthonormal symmetric-matrix bases gives the complete-word
covariance partial derivative.  This is a block of the required joint causal
Jacobian, not that whole Jacobian: variations of mean, generated rows, gains
through those rows, targets, clocks and hard-event branches remain explicit
open inputs. The measured twenty-second gains $0.74261434$ and $0.87382130$
are finite diagnostics in different root/end metrics, not a Poincare
self-inclusion or an all-time magnetic-service theorem.

\paragraph{Structures preserved and relaxation scope.}
The local identities keep the same $P,F,Q,H,R$, the full parity blocks,
Joseph corrections, actual reset sign $G_\theta=I+\tfrac12[d\theta]_\times$,
and additive AW synchronization. The covariance cell and fixed-coefficient
partial derivative are explicitly declared proof relaxations. Moving an $S$
event across a complete sample also crosses accelerometer/reset and possibly
magnetic/AW operations and changes future mean-dependent coefficients; the
local rank bound alone does not certify that full scheduler-word defect.

\subsection{All-time planar guard inactivity in real arithmetic}
The source-specific module and certificate are
\texttt{planar\_service\_guard.py} and
\texttt{planar-service-guard-certificate.json}.
Let $h=1/200$, $\nu=\pi/10<11/35$, and $a(t)$ be the common delivered
specific-force record of the planar pair. Differentiating the \emph{same}
rotated record gives
\[
\|\dot a\|\le .02\nu^3+.02\nu(g+.02\nu^2)
 <106801783/1715000000=:L.
\]
Therefore successive samples differ by at most $hL$.
For the literal 25-Hz first detector, $\gamma=e^{-\pi/4}<23/50$;
the committed rational exponential-series lower bound proves this inequality.
The seeded first high-pass output obeys
\[
\begin{gathered}
h_{1,k}=\gamma(h_{1,k-1}+a_k-a_{k-1}),\quad h_{1,0}=0,\\
\sup_k\|h_{1,k}\|\le\gamma hL/(1-\gamma).
\end{gathered}
\]
The second detector low-pass state is a convex average of $h_1$, starting
at zero, so its high-pass output has norm at most twice this value. The sum
of the three squared-output EWs is a convex average of $\|h_2\|^2$.
Consequently, at every prefix,
\[
\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{RMS}_{\rm detector}&\le\frac{2456441009}{4630500000000}\\
&<0.000531<0.03.
\end{aligned}
\]
The target engagement is zero. Its seeded weight remains zero under the
literal slew and rail parking, and the guard returns the input unchanged.
This proof preserves both detector stages, startup seeding, RMS and weight
chronology. It changes no physical constants and does not require a new
excitation condition. It is an all-time \emph{real-arithmetic component}
result; the float32 rounding transfer and the rest of admission remain open.

\subsection{Generated tuner and clock ports are one-way}
\label{sec:planar-generated-port-structure}
On the deployed default Complementary wave-period input, the adaptation path is
measurement-only.  The literal per-sample order is: commit the candidate staged
on the previous sample; condition the accelerometer; advance the private Mahony
observer; execute the MEKF; read the private vertical channel; stage
$(\tau,\sigma_{aw},R_S)$ from that measurement-only channel; advance the
wave-period/direction stage.  The wave-period input used by the tuner is the
private complementary channel, not the MEKF-levelled ablation.

Therefore the Fr\'echet derivatives from the MEKF mean or covariance to the
generated tuner tuple, to the progress-preserving $S$ period, and to the AW
stationary target are exactly zero on this deployed branch.  The direction
branch may read MEKF attitude and accelerometer bias, but it has no return edge
to the tuner/model schedule.  Thus tuner and clock variation is a one-way
same-history forcing into the covariance recursion; it is not a bidirectional
small-gain loop with $P$.  The remaining bidirectional loop is internal to the
MEKF: $P$ changes $K$ and hence the mean, while attitude/$a_w$ change the
accelerometer and magnetic Jacobians and hence the covariance map.

This structural statement is proved by
\texttt{planar\_generated\_port\_structure.py} and reproduced by
\texttt{planar-generated-port-structure.json}.  It does \emph{not} certify
all-time coefficient ranges, the remaining mean--covariance loop, scheduler
branch containment, or magnetic service.

\subsection{Physical quotient chart and non-promoting word calculation}
\label{sec:planar-quotient-audit}
The shipping attitude chart is a left error on world-to-body rotation.
For $R_{bw}=R_x(\alpha)R_y(\psi)$,
\[
 (\partial_\alpha R_{wb})R_{wb}^T=-[R_y(-\psi)e_x]_\times,
 \qquad \partial_\alpha b_a\big|_{\alpha=0}=g e_y.
\]
Thus an oriented first-order compatibility line has
$r_\theta=R_y(-\psi)e_x$, $r_{b_a}=-g e_y$ and all other coordinates zero.
Indeed with $R=R_y(-\psi)$, $f=R(a_xe_x-ge_z)$ and $B=75Re_x$,
$-[f]_\times r_\theta+r_{b_a}=0$ and $-[B]_\times r_\theta=0$.
This derives the line from physical equations, not singular-vector selection.
The following continuous physical arc integrates this tangent, without
bounding the nominal measurement residual. Write $c=\cos\theta$ and
$n=R_y(-\psi)e_z$. For constant $|\beta|\le\theta$, set
\[
 b_{a,s,\beta}=g\sin\beta\,e_y+g(\cos\beta-c)n.
\]
Substitution cancels both the $e_y$ and variable $\cos\beta$ terms in the
accelerometer record, leaving $R_y(-\psi)(a_xe_x-gce_z)$. The magnetic and
gyro identities are unchanged. Moreover
\[
 \|b_{a,s,\beta}\|^2=g^2(1+c^2-2c\cos\beta)\le g^2\sin^2\theta,
\]
and $\|\dot b_{a,s,\beta}\|\le g(1-c)(.02)\pi/10<3.081\cdot10^{-6}$.
The pitch-extrema gravity chord is $2\cos\beta\sin(.02)$, no smaller than
the already certified endpoint chord. Thus this arc preserves the current
MARINE and SLOW+FAST bounds; only its endpoints have constant accelerometer
bias. The certificate reproduces the formal sensor polynomial identity and
the exact rational membership bounds.

For this principal constant-roll, zero-FAST family, the slow amplitude cap
$B$ implies $\cos\beta\ge C=(1+c^2-(B/g)^2)/(2c)$, hence
$\tan^2(\beta/2)\le(1-C)/(1+C)$ and $|\beta|<.023$ by a rational comparison.
On the constructed arc the sharper $|\beta|<.01$ holds. Relative to the
central physical rotation, the attitude logarithm is exactly
$-\beta R_y(-\psi)e_x$, while the bias remainder from its tangent is
\[
 \eta_b=g(\sin\beta-\beta)e_y+g(\cos\beta-1)n,
 \quad \|\eta_b\|^2\le g^2(\beta^6/36+\beta^4/4).
\]
Conversion into the actual nominal-error and precision chart requires
same-history chart and metric bounds. In particular the physical angle cap
is not a bound on the normalized gauge amplitude, and this curved fibre is
not replaced by its tangent line.

Deterministic prefix induction gives identical complete estimator executions
along this physical arc. Its total estimator/P variation is zero. A secant
formed by perturbing the nominal root at fixed record is a different
variation, so its gauge-to-P block is not that total physical derivative.
This distinction does not remove $C_Q\alpha$ or the linked physical forcing
from the error word. Physical magnetic probe directions also vary with
$\beta$; no all-time service follows from record identity alone.

For actual SPD endpoint covariances $P_i=L_iL_i^T$, put
$u_i=L_i^{-1}r_i/\|L_i^{-1}r_i\|$, and let $U_i$ be an orthonormal
complement. In raw coordinates the precision-orthogonal gauge projector is
$L_i u_i u_i^T L_i^{-1}=\bar r_i\bar r_i^TP_i^{-1}$, where
$\bar r_i^TP_i^{-1}\bar r_i=1$.
For a supplied affine word $e_N=Me_0+b$, direct substitution gives exactly
\[
\begin{split}
 \xi_N&=M_Q\xi_0+b_Q+C_Q\alpha_0,\\
 M_Q&=U_N^TL_N^{-1}ML_0U_0,\qquad
 C_Q=U_N^TL_N^{-1}ML_0u_0,\\
 b_Q&=U_N^TL_N^{-1}b.
\end{split}
\]
Whitened projector checks are dimensionless; an absolute residual in
$\Pi^TJ-J\Pi$ depends on covariance units and falsely rejected the finite
native word. The same numerical tolerance is retained in the whitened audit.
No such floating identity check is an interval theorem.

\textbf{FINITE DIAGNOSTIC ONLY.} On the exported 20-second word the
